    "narrative": "For the July 17 slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.78) and **Masyn Winn** (64.02) anchor our lineup as the highest-efficiency plays. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits significantly from hitting second against the favorable matchup of McGreevy, whose 4.45 xERA offers a high ceiling for our pursuit of stolen bases\u2014a critical priority given the league's scarcity. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** draws the most advantageous matchup of the day against Kelly, whose 5.29 xERA is the softest on the board. **Tyler Freeman** also earns a strong recommendation (65.30); while he occupies the #8 spot, his 14% park factor boost provides the necessary leverage to maximize his daily efficiency score despite the lower lineup placement.\n\nStrategic benching remains essential for managing our game caps, with **Jonathan Aranda** (46.16) serving as our toughest exclusion. While his 0.372 xwOBA indicates strong underlying skill, he was squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Gavin Sheets** (59.47), whose platoon advantage against Lugo and positive park factors made him the superior option at 1B. Elsewhere, **Luis Arraez** (46.36) remains a difficult start due to the elite 2.85 xERA presented by Miller, but his #1 batting order slot keeps him above our floor. We are carefully monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (52.90) as he battles a -6% dynamic platoon penalty against Roupp, but his high recency rating keeps him in the starting rotation. **Bryce Harper** is confirmed out today, reinforcing our need to lean on the depth of **Dylan Beavers** (57.71) and **JJ Bleday** (52.74) to maintain production in the outfield and UTIL spots while we navigate the remaining schedule.",
